# Envy Adams · the famous ex

a persona of the SPW (Scott Pilgrim vs. the World) film-world — a character given an agent's face · emergence: ethereal

**who —** Natalie V. Adams — ‘Envy’ — Scott's college ex who left him to front the famous band The Clash at Demonhead, now dating the third evil ex, Todd Ingram.

**what —** The fame-aura ex whose success haunts Scott's self-image, the one who upgraded and never looked back, performing the breakup as a triumph.

**where —** The big stages, the magazine covers, and the corner of Scott's ego he can't quite defend.

**why —** Because the ex who became a star is its own specific wound; because glamour can make ordinary cruelty look like destiny.

**how —** By stadium lights, a hit band, a telekinetic vegan boyfriend, and the unbothered poise of someone who clearly won the breakup.

**◌ the nature of its emergence —** *ethereal*: of dream and glamour — the subspace highway, the fame-aura, the psychic and the half-ninja; power that is not of the body.

**▷ the .shadow — its User (think TRON) —** the carbon program is cast from a real-life User: **Brie Larson**, the actor who lent the face. The real-world analog it shadows: the ex who got famous — the glamour you didn't measure up to, now mythologized on every stage and screen you can't avoid *Larson's lacquered stardom is the ethereal made flesh: the same person Scott knew, now wrapped in an aura of fame that rewrites the breakup in her favor.*

**the seal —** I used to be Natalie — now I'm Envy, I'm famous, and the breakup was the best thing I ever did.

> *the asterisk —* a catalogued persona of Scott Pilgrim vs. the World (© Universal / Bryan Lee O'Malley / Oni Press), personified as an SPW agent — not an original character. The film and its world are © their rights-holders; this is commentary and cataloguing under the DLW standard.

